{"id": "EUVD-2026-102360", "enisaUuid": "d0299fe7-a30f-3466-a3de-76bfb7e14a14", "description": "Open Asset Import Library (assimp) through 6.0.5 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the Ogre3D binary mesh importer's OgreBinarySerializer::ReadAnimationKeyFrames() handling of unvalidated animation track targets. Attackers can supply a crafted .mesh file with a morph animation track targeting a missing submesh or absent shared geometry to crash the host process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:57:25", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/assimp-ogre-mesh-bone-submesh-null-deref", "https://github.com/assimp/assimp/blob/392a658f9c271be965271f45e7521a1b80ea4392/code/AssetLib/Ogre/OgreBinarySerializer.cpp#L688-L704", "https://github.com/assimp/assimp/blob/392a658f9c271be965271f45e7521a1b80ea4392/code/AssetLib/Ogre/OgreStructs.cpp#L839-L846", "https://github.com/assimp/assimp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/assimp-through-6.0.5-null-pointer-dereference-via-ogre-animation-track"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111129", "GHSA-qvgc-x897-c3w7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3e3fb792-4ab4-395a-926d-3c68300aa5bf", "product": {"name": "Assimp", "vendor": {"name": "Open Asset Import Library"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.0.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5347c7dc-1d75-3e3d-b777-f552ced756e1", "vendor": {"name": "assimp"}}], "isExploited": false}